{
  "Band headers": "",
  "A band is a header over several columns (band column): give it a `title` and the `columns` under it — columns and other bands, to any depth. The header becomes a row per level of bands over the columns' own titles, each band spanning its columns. Drag a column: it moves only inside its band; drag a band: its columns go with it. A band is pinned, hidden and moved as a whole, from its own menu (its header's button, Alt+Down) or with `columnOption` by its `name`. Here “Payment” sits over three columns and “Order” over two columns and the “Delivery” band.": "",
  "Band field": "",
  "The band’s caption and what sits under it: columns and bands, to any depth. A band holds no data.": "",
  "`band-` and its place": "",
  "Its identity in the layout, `columnOption`, `columnSettings` and the events (`band-1`, `band-1-2` when it has none).": "",
  "Bands given flat’s `customizeColumns` does: a band with `isBand`, and columns (or bands) that name it in `ownerBand`, by `name` or by its place in `columns`.": "",
  "the `bandAlign` setting": "",
  "Where the caption sits over its columns.": "",
  "The band pinned, or hidden, with all its columns. A column inside a band takes its band’s side; pinning it pins the band.": "",
  "the grid’s settings": "",
  "What the user may do with the band: drag it among its neighbours, hide it, pin it, open its menu.": "",
  "Content of your own in the band’s header, made once; `ctx.band`, `ctx.title`.": "",
  "Where the captions sit when a band does not say.": "",
  "How bands do it": "",
  "A column moves only among the columns and bands of its own band, a band among those beside it, both inside their pinned zone and not across one that cannot move (`movable: false`), by dragging the header, with “Move” in the menu and the arrow keys, or with `columnOption(name, 'visibleIndex', n)`.": "",
  "The columns are resized as always (the edge of a column’s header, a double-click fits it); a band follows its columns.": "",
  "A band’s header does not sort and has no filter: its columns do, as before.": "",
  "Hiding every column of a band hides the band; hiding a band (its menu, `columnOption(name, 'visible', false)`) hides its columns. The last shown column stays.": "",
  "With bands the list of columns is a tree with check boxes, the bands over their columns; a band’s check box shows or hides all of them.": "",
  "`grid.layout` keeps the columns’ order, widths and hidden state, and `bands` with each band’s hidden state and side; a band’s place comes from its columns. A layout that tears a band apart puts it together where its first column is. `layoutKey` keeps it all.": "",
  "CSV writes a line per level of bands above the titles, each band’s title over its first column; `exportSheet()` adds header rows, and `merges` names the cells a band (and a column down the band rows) spans for the writer to merge.": "",
  "Only the header changes: the rows, the virtual list and paging are as before.": "",
  "Band rows are `row`s of `columnheader`s in the head's row group: a band's header carries the `aria-colindex` of its first column and `aria-colspan` its columns, the columns keep their own index, and the band rows count in `aria-rowindex` and `aria-rowcount`. Over a pinned column no band covers an empty piece stays with the column, so the band rows scroll under it.": "",
  "Adaptive columns": "",
  "With `settings.columnHidingEnabled` the grid hides columns while it is narrower than they are, the last one first; with a `hidingPriority` on some columns only those hide, the lowest first. A “…” column then opens a row's adaptive detail under it: the hidden columns' titles and values (editors where the row can be edited), one row at a time. It is worked out from the column widths and the grid's width (a `ResizeObserver`), never from what it draws, and again whenever either changes: drag the splitter. The hidden columns still count as shown — the column chooser, `getVisibleColumns()`, the export and copying have them.": "",
  "Columns hide while the grid is narrower than they are, the last one first, and show in the rows’ adaptive detail.": "",
  "Given on any column, only columns with one hide (without `columnHidingEnabled` too), the lowest first. Pinned and grouped columns never hide.": "",
  "How the detail lays out its form (the kit’s `FormLayout`).": "",
  "Editors instead of texts for the cells the user can fill, in the `row`, `cell` and `batch` edit modes; they write into the row’s draft as its cells do.": "",
  "Editing a row whose hidden columns it can fill opens its detail, and leaving the row closes it again (the `row` edit mode).": "",
  "The “…” column’s width; the keys on its cell that open and close the detail.": "",
  "The detail is a row of its own right after its row, before the row's master-detail when both are open (order): measured as it is drawn, in the reading order (`aria-owns`), counted in `aria-rowindex`, its one cell named “Hidden columns of row 3” (`gridAdaptiveOf`; `gridAdaptive` names the “…” and its column). Grouped rows, paging and the virtual list keep it under its row; a wider grid with nothing hidden closes it.": "",
  "To its band’s header; again to the band above.": "",
  "To the first column or band under it.": "",
  "Along the bands of its row.": "",
  "Its menu: pin, move, hide the band, the column chooser, reset.": "",
  "Opens or closes the row’s adaptive detail.": "",
  "Into the detail; from its last stop into the row’s master-detail, or, while the row is edited, on to the next row’s cells.": "",
  "Into the editors of its open adaptive detail.": "",
  "Back to the row.": "",
  "A row’s detail is about to lay out its form, when it opens and again when other columns hide or show: change `formOptions` (`items` — the hidden fields, or kit form items —, `colCount`, `minColWidth`, `labelMode`).": "",
  "A row’s detail is about to open or close, from its “…”, its keys or code; `cancel` keeps it as it is.": "",
  "It opened or closed.": "",
  "Opens a row’s detail by its key (the one open closes first), or closes the one open.": "",
  "Whether that row’s detail is open. Reactive.": "",
  "`string[]`, reactive": "",
  "The columns the width hides now, in display order.": "",
  "`grid.adaptiveDetail.colCount = 1`; `onOptionChanged` tells `adaptiveDetail.colCount`.": "",
  "The open detail right after its row, `rowType: 'detailAdaptive'`, before the row's master-detail.": ""
}
